{
  "id": "80864",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Ksp and Gram Solubility Calculations",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Note that solubility is not always given as a molar value. When the solubility of a compound is given in units other than moles per liter, we must convert the solubility into moles per liter (i.e., molarity) in order to use it in the solubility product expression. The following example shows how to perform those unit conversions before determining the solubility product equilibrium."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ohvphxonxodamd2",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2459603328",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "365304075",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "border": "hidden",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "Many of the pigments used by artists in oil-based paints are sparingly soluble in water. For example, the solubility of the artist’s pigment chrome yellow, PbCrO"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "4"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": ", is 4.6 × 10"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "–6"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": " g/L. Determine the value of K"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "sp"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": " for PbCrO"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "4"
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "."
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "ybl487s56l7dona",
                            "type": "p"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "fsdtxbua2zmsyej",
                        "type": "td"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "alt": "A photograph is shown of a portion of an oil painting which reveals colors of orange, brown, yellow, green, blue, and purple colors in its strokes. A few water droplets rest on the surface.",
                            "caption": [
                              {
                                "children": [
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "Oil paints contain pigments that are very slightly soluble in water. In addition to chrome yellow (PbCrO"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "sub": true,
                                    "text": "4"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "), examples include Prussian blue (Fe"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "sub": true,
                                    "text": "7"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "(CN)"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "sub": true,
                                    "text": "18"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "), the reddish-orange color vermilion (HgS), and green color veridian (Cr"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "sub": true,
                                    "text": "2"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "O"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "sub": true,
                                    "text": "3"
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "em": true,
                                    "text": "). (Credit: Sonny Abesamis.)"
                                  }
                                ],
                                "type": "p"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "id": "lfumztgsq9evj8u",
                                "text": " ",
                                "type": "text"
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "axp8ppqw18uv412",
                            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/f5/f55b1a94fe78dd8a54bfd316645414db/CNX_Chem_15_01_OilPaints.jpg",
                            "type": "img",
                            "width": "375"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "ogwxmzjzgakq0jn",
                        "type": "td"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "7ck4zqdoo33d4y7",
                    "type": "tr"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vqwhxiam3zd2yfr",
                "type": "table"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We are given the solubility of PbCrO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in grams per liter. If we convert this solubility into moles per liter, we can find the equilibrium concentrations of Pb"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and CrO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", then "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sp"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "isjun7qrzmws0rt",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Use the molar mass of PbCrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ("
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": ""
                              }
                            ],
                            "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                            "src": "\\frac{323.2\\;\\mathrm g}{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}})",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula_inline"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " to convert the solubility of PbCrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " in grams per liter into moles per liter: "
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " ",
                                "type": "text"
                              }
                            ],
                            "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                            "src": "\\lbrack{\\mathrm{PbCrO}}_4\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\frac{4.6\\times10^{-6}\\;\\mathrm g\\;{\\mathrm{PbCrO}}_4}{1\\;\\mathrm L} \\;\\times\\;\\frac{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;{\\mathrm{PbCrO}}_4}{323.2\\;\\mathrm g\\;{\\mathrm{PbCrO}}_4}\\;=\\;1.4\\times10^{-8}\\; \\frac{\\mathrm{mol}}{\\mathrm L}",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula_inline"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " "
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "186341326",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "8yfmbsypnaj4jy0",
                    "type": "li"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "The equation for the dissolution indicates that 1 mole of PbCrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " gives 1 mole of Pb"
                          },
                          {
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "2+"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "("
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "text": "aq"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ") and 1 mol of CrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "2−"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "("
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "text": "aq"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "):"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "jg1i5u555ju9nwy",
                        "type": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " ",
                                "type": "text"
                              }
                            ],
                            "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                            "src": "{\\mathrm{PbCrO}}_4(s)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{CrO}}_4^{2-}(aq)",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula_inline"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "wtmla5fxxslu7sz",
                        "type": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Therefore, both [Pb"
                          },
                          {
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "2+"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "] and [CrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "2−"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "] are equal to the molar solubility of PbCrO"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "4"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ":"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "p5tm9v85lg051mg",
                        "type": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " ",
                                "type": "text"
                              }
                            ],
                            "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                            "src": "\\lbrack\\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\lbrack{\\mathrm{CrO}}_4^{2-}\\rbrack\\;=\\;1.4\\times10^{-8}\\;\\mathrm M",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula_inline"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "d56egi3ftdrtkc8",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "kzzl4pzao1t9v0t",
                    "type": "li"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Substitute these values into the solubility product expression to determine "
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "text": "K"
                          },
                          {
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "sp"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ":"
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "ehwgmn2v4xl77vd",
                        "type": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " ",
                                "type": "text"
                              }
                            ],
                            "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                            "src": "K_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\;=\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{CrO}_4^{2-}\\rbrack\\; =\\;(1.4\\times10^{–8})(1.4\\times10^{–8})\\;=\\;2.0\\times10^{–16}",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula_inline"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "pm3j63mv0kaofrd",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "o1fpqsjlchvhm8d",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xwy19gi2taua35m",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
